      "text": "```\nWIRE BONDING — LEGACY, STILL DOMINANT FOR COST SEGMENTS"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-PACKAGING.md#009",
      "path": [
        "07-PACKAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging, git-history:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging]",
        "canonical_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[packaging]",
        "current_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiconductor-manufacturing:packaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiconductor-manufacturing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[packaging]",
        "section": "semiconductor-manufacturing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Packaging - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MECHANISM:\n  Gold (Au) or copper (Cu) or aluminum (Al) wire (15-75 µm diameter)\n  Thermosonic bonding (heat + ultrasonic + pressure):\n    Ball bond: wire melts → gold ball → bonded to die pad (Al bond pad)\n    Stitch bond: wedge bond to package substrate or leadframe\n    Result: electrical connection from die pad to package terminal"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-PACKAGING.md#010",
      "path": [
        "07-PACKAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging, git-history:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging]",
        "canonical_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[packaging]",
        "current_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiconductor-manufacturing:packaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiconductor-manufacturing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[packaging]",
        "section": "semiconductor-manufacturing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Packaging - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PROCESS:\n  Die flip face-up → attach to substrate (epoxy or solder)\n  Capillary tool: form ball → position over die pad → press + ultrasonic\n  → Pull wire arc → form stitch on substrate pad → clip wire\n  High-speed: 10-20 bonds/second per machine head"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-PACKAGING.md#011",
      "path": [
        "07-PACKAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging, git-history:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging]",
        "canonical_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[packaging]",
        "current_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiconductor-manufacturing:packaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiconductor-manufacturing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[packaging]",
        "section": "semiconductor-manufacturing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Packaging - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PITCH LIMITATION:\n  Bond pad pitch: 40-60 µm (fine pitch) down to ~25 µm (ultra-fine)\n  Wire span: up to 5 mm (longer → sagging, cross-shorting risk)"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-PACKAGING.md#012",
      "path": [
        "07-PACKAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging, git-history:semiconductor-manufacturing:07-packaging]",
        "canonical_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[packaging]",
        "current_path": "semiconductor-manufacturing/07-PACKAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiconductor-manufacturing:packaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
