        "title": "Packaging - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "C4 BUMPS (Controlled Collapse Chip Connection — IBM, 1964):\n  Solder bumps on die: SnPb (old) → lead-free SnAgCu (SAC) solder\n  Bump diameter: 50-250 µm (area-array across full die surface)\n  Pitch: 100-200 µm (peripheral) or 150-250 µm (area array) for traditional FC\n  Micro-bumps (advanced): 20-50 µm diameter at 40-100 µm pitch"
    },
